Task review is back. One Important finding to fix. It was labeled plan-mandated, I took it to Sven, and he ruled that the finding governs over the plan text — so you are authorised to replace the test the brief pinned.

**Finding — `gate_withholds_later_chunks_until_released` is vacuous on a slow machine, and leaves the property Tasks 9 and 11 depend on unasserted.**

`assert!(!handle.is_finished())` after a 200 ms sleep is one-directional: on a machine where a loopback round trip exceeds the window, a completely broken gate passes. The trailing full-body `assert_eq!` does not rescue it, because with a broken gate the body is byte-identical. And nothing asserts the pre-gate chunk *reached the client* — you verified that property with a temporary raw-socket test and then deleted it, so it is currently asserted nowhere in the committed suite. If a future change withholds the pre-gate bytes, all four tests stay green while every cancel-mid-stream scenario in Tasks 9 and 11 fires its cancellation before the client has seen a single byte. That is the same vacuity class you just fixed in test 4.

**Replace it with a three-part test**, shape approved by Sven:

```
let mut frames = response.bytes_stream();

// (a) the pre-gate chunk really arrived — fails LOUDLY on a slow machine
//     instead of passing silently
let prefix = timeout(WINDOW, accumulate_until(&mut frames, "data: one\n\n")).await;
assert!(prefix.is_ok(), "pre-gate chunk never reached the client");

// (b) the gate withholds the next frame
assert!(timeout(WINDOW, frames.next()).await.is_err(),
        "gate did not withhold the post-gate chunk");

// (c) release delivers the remainder
gate.release();
assert_eq!(drain(&mut frames).await, "data: two\n\n");
```

